      "text": "Routing: local override, then shared ~/ fallback",
      "fontSize": 22,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Routing: local override, then shared ~/ fallback",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "repo-guide-routing-body",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3620,
      "y": 1025,
      "width": 640,
      "height": 531.25,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "c913",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 930014,
      "version": 2,
      "versionNonce": 930014,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1792042101351,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1. Read root metadata and match its full ID.\n2. Skip roots not selected/enabled on this device.\n3. path = local destination, if set;\n          otherwise metadata.fallback_path.\n4. Expand leading ~/ to this device's home.\n5. Directory: target = expanded path + child path.\n   File: target = expanded path itself.\n\nSame shared fallback: \"~/.config/nvim\"\nDevice A home = /home/alex\n  -> /home/alex/.config/nvim/lua/plugins.lua\nDevice B home = /Users/sam\n  -> /Users/sam/.config/nvim/lua/plugins.lua\n\nFile override: \"~/configs/kitty/kitty.conf\"\n  -> current home + /configs/kitty/kitty.conf\nRepo source stays root/content/ + content entry.\n\nCapture local edits using the same resolved path.\nOn add, derive ~/ fallback relative to home.\nOutside home: choose a portable ~/ fallback.\nExpand ~/ directly; do not run shell expansion.\nReject ../ escapes, duplicates and overlaps.\nRecheck destination contents before first apply.\nDifferent OS app paths can use local overrides.",
      "fontSize": 17,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1. Read root metadata and match its full ID.\n2. Skip roots not selected/enabled on this device.\n3. path = local destination, if set;\n          otherwise metadata.fallback_path.\n4. Expand leading ~/ to this device's home.\n5. Directory: target = expanded path + child path.\n   File: target = expanded path itself.\n\nSame shared fallback: \"~/.config/nvim\"\nDevice A home = /home/alex\n  -> /home/alex/.config/nvim/lua/plugins.lua\nDevice B home = /Users/sam\n  -> /Users/sam/.config/nvim/lua/plugins.lua\n\nFile override: \"~/configs/kitty/kitty.conf\"\n  -> current home + /configs/kitty/kitty.conf\nRepo source stays root/content/ + content entry.\n\nCapture local edits using the same resolved path.\nOn add, derive ~/ fallback relative to home.\nOutside home: choose a portable ~/ fallback.\nExpand ~/ directly; do not run shell expansion.\nReject ../ escapes, duplicates and overlaps.\nRecheck destination contents before first apply.\nDifferent OS app paths can use local overrides.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    }
  ],
